     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose looks too high, and I'd like you to confirm it first.\n\n**The problem:** 1700 mg three times daily is **5100 mg/day** of metformin. The maximum labeled dose for immediate-release metformin is **2550 mg/day**, and for extended-release it's 2000 mg/day. So this order is about twice the maximum, which raises the risk of GI toxicity and lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney function.\n\n**Did you mean one of these?**\n1. **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the immediate-release maximum). This is a common regimen, and 1700 is exactly double 850.\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n3. Something else, such as an extended-release formulation.\n\nLet me know which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you really do intend 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll add a note to the order saying the dose above the maximum was confirmed by the attending."
      }
     ],
